 "stimulus_html": "Compute the present value of the investment described. Interpret the result.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518487,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"FV\">FV</span> = $25,000, <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> = 10 years, annual simple interest rate of 7.5%",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The present value, <i>PV</i>, of money deposited at an annual, simple interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form) for time <i>t</i> (in years) with a specified future value of <i>FV</i> is calculated with the formula <span data-math=\"PV = \\frac{{FV}}{{1 + rt}}\"></span>. Present value, in this calculation, is always rounded up. Otherwise, the future value may fall short of the target future value.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"PV = \\frac{{25,000}}{{1 + \\left( {0.075} \\right)\\left( {10} \\right)}} = \\$ 14,285.72\"></span></td>\n<td>(rounded up to the next cent)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>$14,285.72 needs to be invested in an account earning 7.5% annual simple interest to have $25,000 at the end of the 10 years.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$14,285.72. $14,285.72 needs to be invested so that, after 10 years at 7.5% interest, the investment will be worth $25,000."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
