     "content_html": "<p>The present value, <i>PV</i>, of money deposited at an annual, simple interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form) for time <i>t</i> (in years) with a specified future value of <i>FV</i> is calculated with the formula <span data-math=\"PV = \\frac{{FV}}{{1 + rt}}\"></span>. Present value, in this calculation, is always rounded up. Otherwise, the future value may fall short of the target future value.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"PV = \\frac{{320,000}}{{1 + \\left( {0.065} \\right)\\left( {35} \\right)}} = \\$ 97,709.93\"></span></td>\n<td>(rounded up to the next cent)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>$97,709.93 needs to be invested in an account earning 6.5% annual simple interest to have $320,000 at the end of the 35 years.</p>"
