   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The present value, <i>PV</i>, of money deposited at an annual, simple interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form) for time <i>t</i> (in years) with a specified future value of <i>FV</i> is calculated with the formula <span data-math=\"PV = \\frac{{FV}}{{1 + rt}}\"></span>. Present value, in this calculation, is always rounded up. Otherwise, the future value may fall short of the target future value.</p>\n<p>270 months is 22.5 years.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"PV = \\frac{{90,000}}{{1 + \\left( {0.0375} \\right)\\left( {22.5} \\right)}} = \\$ 48,813.56\"></span></td>\n<td>(rounded up to the next cent)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>$48,813.56 needs to be invested in an account earning 3.75% annual simple interest to have $90,000 at the end of the 22.5 years.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$48,813.56. $48,813.56 needs to be invested so that, after 270 months at 3.75% interest, the investment will be worth $90,000."
    }
   ],
